From f745a0f412d73f18882c817b31df24bb10809166 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 20:21:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(cart): automatic cross-pillar bundle discount
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Implements CLAUDE.md §7.2's 2026-09-10 amendment: a cart containing at
least one Tea-pillar line and one Masala-pillar line automatically
gets a bundle discount, applied as a distinct server-computed
crossPillarDiscountPaise line in lib/commerce/pricing.ts's
PricingResult — never folded into discountPaise/couponCode, and never
touching the coupons/coupon_redemptions tables (this is structural and
automatic, not a manually-entered code).

- Rate is read from settings ("cross_pillar_bundle_discount_percent",
  default 10%) via a new getCrossPillarBundleDiscountPercent query,
  following the exact pattern of getFreeShippingThresholdPaise. The
  10% default is a PLACEHOLDER flagged for real client confirmation,
  same status as content/home.ts's founderStory draft copy.
- Discount = percent% off the single cheapest unit in the cart (chosen
  over a coupons-style max_discount_paise cap as the simpler, more
  defensible option — easy for a shopper to verify by eye).
- lib/nav.ts's TEA_COLLECTION_SLUGS/MASALA_COLLECTION_SLUGS are now
  exported and reused for pillar classification, instead of a second
  list.
- VariantPricingRow/PricingLine gain collectionSlug (joined from
  `collections` in lib/db/queries/variants.ts) so pricing.ts can
  classify each line without a second query.
- orders.bundle_discount_paise (migration 0011) snapshots the applied
  amount per order, separate from discount_paise, mirroring how the
  schema already keeps discount and shipping as distinct columns.
- Cart drawer/page (via OrderSummary) shows the applied discount as
  its own "Tea + Masala bundle discount" row when active.
- PDP's "you may also like" section links to the other pillar's
  primary collection ("Add a <Pillar> favourite and save").
- Server-recomputed like every other pricing figure (CLAUDE.md §7.5):
  PricingInput has no field a client could use to supply a discount
  amount at all.

Vitest coverage added: no discount for single-pillar carts (Tea-only
and Masala-only), discount applied for a cross-pillar cart, discount
scales with the configured settings percent (not a literal), discount
drops when the qualifying line is out of stock, and an explicit
"client cannot supply a discount" case documenting why tampering isn't
even expressible in PricingInput's shape.

